  "about": {
    "title": "About the Artist",
    "content": [
      "I've been drawing since childhood, but it wasn't until I discovered hyperrealistic portraiture that I found my true calling. Through pencil and paper, I strive to capture not just faces, but stories—every line, shadow, and highlight carefully crafted to preserve moments that matter.",
      "Based in Nairobi, I've had the honor of creating portraits for Kenya's most influential leaders, from Deputy Prime Minister Musalia Mudavadi to activist Boniface Mwangi. But whether I'm drawing a public figure or a family's cherished memory, every portrait receives the same dedication to detail and excellence.",
      "Each piece takes 8-12 hours of focused work, using professional-grade materials to ensure your portrait will last generations. I believe in the power of art to preserve legacies, celebrate milestones, and tell the stories that make us who we are."
    ],
